5. System Architecture (Failure‑Resilient)

```
USER PROMPT
│
▼
SCHEMA RETRIEVAL LAYER
  ├─ fetch table names, columns, keys from information_schema
  └─ for >50 tables : activate Schema RAG (vector retrieval)
│
▼
CONTEXT ASSEMBLY LAYER
  ├─ inject schema subset + user role + query history
  └─ role‑scoped VIEW definitions applied
│
▼
LLM REASONING LAYER (SQL generation)
  └─ entity‑to‑column mapping with ambiguity resolution
│
▼
CONFIDENCE SCORING & CIRCUIT BREAKER          ← NEW
  ├─ LLM self‑assessment: “Am I >95 % confident this SQL matches the intent?”
  ├─ if NO → return clarification question to user
  └─ EXPLAIN ANALYZE cost check (rows scanned, cost)
        if cost > threshold → abort, suggest narrowing
│
▼
POLICY ENFORCEMENT ENGINE (formerly SQL Guard)
  ├─ AST parsing via sqlglot: forbid DROP, DELETE, INSERT, ALTER, EXEC, etc.
  ├─ read‑only DB connection (fallback enforcement)
  ├─ row‑level permission injection (WHERE clauses based on role)
  └─ export policy check (none / watermarked / unrestricted)
│
▼
DATABASE EXECUTION (PostgreSQL / MySQL)
│
▼
STRUCTURED JSON OUTPUT
│
▼
DYNAMIC UI GENERATOR
  ├─ sortable table, summary cards (auto‑typed)
  ├─ EXPLAINABILITY PANEL: “How did I get this?” (mapped columns, filters, rows scanned)
  └─ export controls enforced client‑side
│
▼
EPHEMERAL DASHBOARD (session‑bound, Redis TTL)
│
▼
SESSION DESTRUCTION + DIFFERENTIAL AUDIT LOG (persistent, minimised)
```

Failure‑mode handling (every stage has a fallback):

· Schema fetch fails → show “Database unreachable – try again or contact admin”.
· LLM timeout → fall back to cached schema suggestions, prompt user to refine question.
· Policy engine rejects SQL → return “Your question cannot be executed due to security policies. Please rephrase or request access.”
· Cost exceeds threshold → “This query would scan 4.2 M rows. Add a date range or department filter.”
· UI render fails → clean error state, session still destroyed; audit log captures the failure.

